This is a browser side server JS example. It's an adaptation/simplification of [1] to our
Printer interface using a generic BidirAdapter (../../bidir-adapter).

The BidirAdapter allows any Ice client to indirectly invoke objects living in the
browser.

This example shows invocation from browser to standard Ice Server (C++, Python, ...)
and viceversa.

Procedure:

- Install DEPENDS
- Run bidir-adapter:
  bidir-adapter$ make start

- Run the browser object:
  js/hello$ make run-server

- Open http://localhost:8080, click "Start" and copy the object proxy.

- Run a Printer client (any language) using the shown proxy:
  py/hello$ ./client.py "<proxy>"

- Invocations are shown in webpage


[1] https://github.com/zeroc-ice/ice-demos/tree/3.7/js/Ice/bidir
